<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n17003" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀτέλ-εστος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>without end, issue,</i> or
				<i>effect, unaccomplished,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἅλιον θεῖναι πόνον ἠδ᾽ ἀ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					4.26
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				57
			</span></i>,<i><span class="en">
				168
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Od.
				2.273
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σῖτον ἔδοντες μὰψ αὔτως ἀ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					16.111
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὰ δέ κεν θεὸς ἢ τελέσειεν ἤ κ᾽
					ἀτέλεστ᾽ εἴη</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					8.571
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				<u>Tab.Defix.Aud.</u>
				68b
			</span></i>: rare in Prose, of prayers, <i>not deserving of
				accomplishment,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Antipho
				1.22
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀ. κῶνος</span>
			<i>truncated</i> cone, <i><span class="en">
				Hero
			</span></i>
			<i>*Stereom.</i><i><span class="en">
				1.16
			</span></i>: neut. pl. as Adv., <i>inconclusively,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀ. λαλεῖν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>AP</u>
					12.21
				</span></i>
			 (<i><span class="en">
				Strat.
			</span></i>). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>uninitiated in.</i> . , c. gen., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">βακχευμάτων</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					E.
					<u>Ba.</u>
					40
				</span></i>
			: metaph., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀ. ἱερῶν καὶ μυστηρίων τῆς πολιτείας</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Plu.
					<u>Flam.</u>
					2
				</span></i>
			: abs., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀ. καὶ ἀμύητος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pl.
					<u>Phd.</u>
					69c
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>Rh.</u>
				1419a4
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Phld.
				<u>Acad.Ind.</u>
				p.4
			</span></i> M.; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀ. τῷ θεῷ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Ael.
					<u>VH</u>
					3.9
				</span></i>
			; prob. <i>unmarried, Tab. Defix.Aud.</i><i><span class="en">
				68a
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>III.</b>
			
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀτελής</span>
			 III, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">χώρα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					D.
					<u>Prooem.</u>
					55
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>IV.</b>
			<i>endless, eternal,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Parm.
				8.4
			</span></i>.</div>
